WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.773
Summarizing a distribution with a few moments makes
it tractable to visualize and,

00:00:03.853 --> 00:00:07.627
crucially, to predict from first principles.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:11.480
For example,

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.333
the full densities of hadronic jets cannot be
computed in perturbative QCD,

00:00:15.413 --> 00:00:19.187
but the energy dependence of their moments can be.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:23.040
Unbinned unfolding methods already exist and avoid
binning artifacts,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.893
but they are built to unfold entire spectra,

00:00:26.973 --> 00:00:30.747
so they may trade away precision on the handful of
moments a physicist actually wants.

00:00:30.827 --> 00:00:34.600
This motivates a dedicated method that unfolds the
moments themselves.
